{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Eggs of.</b> He compared them to viper eggs, for when they break open:" "<b>And the webs [of the spider].</b> Known from the spider's behavior." "<b>Who eats of their eggs.</b> Of viper eggs." "<b>And the one who crushes.</b> It should have had a kamatz gadol under the resh, but this word is unusual, like ולנה in the midst of his house (Zechariah 5:4). Now והזורה is a paʿul form, like כי מולים היו (Joshua 5:4), סוגה בשושנים (Song of Songs 7:3); it is from the root of ויזר את הגזה (Judges 6:38), for whoever crushes it, then the viper breaks open and an efa comes forth, like אפעה ושרף (Isaiah 30:6)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:16.273257412Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}